<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates steady to softer.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates steady to softer.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were steady to lower on Thursday, reflecting the high liquidty in the system, traders said.</p>
<p>The one to two-week, and 12-month rates dipped, while the rest were steady. Only the three-month rate slightly rose.</p>
<p>Overall, PHIBOR showed the soft interest rates on the peso in the light of the steady inflow of dollars which is increasing peso liquidity, a foreign bank dealer said.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  MARCH 6		 MARCH 5</p>
<p>    1 W		9  1/2		  9  5/8</p>
<p>    2 W		9  1/2		  9  5/8</p>
<p>    1 M		9 11/16		 9 11/16</p>
<p>    2 M		9  3/4		  9  3/4</p>
<p>    3 M		9  7/8		  9 13/16</p>
<p>    6 M		10  1/16		10  1/16</p>
<p>    12M		10  1/4		 10  5/16</p>
<p>    VAL		7-Mar		   6-Mar</p>
<p>--LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
